<p class="hint center">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>The method behind the numbers</h2>
<p>This calculator applies straight-line depreciation, age divided by expected life, capped at the maximum you select. Real estimates may adjust for condition, use different life tables or treat some items, such as permits or debris removal, as non-depreciable. Treat the result as a planning figure.</p>
<h2>Common life expectancies</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Typical range</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>Laminated asphalt shingles</th><td>25–30 years</td></tr><tr><th>Three-tab shingles</th><td>15–25 years</td></tr><tr><th>Standing-seam metal roofing</th><td>40–60 years</td></tr><tr><th>Vinyl siding</th><td>30–40 years</td></tr><tr><th>Interior paint</th><td>8–12 years</td></tr><tr><th>Carpet</th><td>8–12 years</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2>Collecting the holdback</h2>
<p>Most replacement cost policies pay recoverable depreciation once repairs are complete, often within a set number of days. Send the insurer invoices and photos of the finished work. Our <a href="/policy-math-tools/idaho-claim-timeline-builder/">claim timeline builder</a> can remind you before that window closes.</p>

<h2>Questions about the RCV vs ACV calculator</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can labor be depreciated?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Practices differ by policy and jurisdiction. Ask the insurer to explain in writing how its estimate treats labor depreciation.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if I decide not to repair?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Under most replacement cost policies you keep the ACV payment but may not collect the held-back depreciation.</p></div></details></div>
